<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indian Ocean</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indian Ocean is the world's third-largest ocean, bounded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monsoon">monsoon</a> winds made it one of the oldest and busiest arenas of long-distance maritime trade. Many empires drew wealth from it, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a>, while the Portuguese and British empires sought to dominate its sea routes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indian-ocean.jpg" alt="Indian Ocean" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Central Intelligence Agency · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_Ocean-CIA_WFB_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
